      "content": "\"Stopping the pressure\" means finding a way to let go of the impossible expectation that you have to be perfect for everyone else. It's not about letting everything fall apart; it's about recognizing that you are not the only thing holding up the world. That peace you crave—the one where you don't have to perform—is possible, but it requires a radical, quiet surrender to the fact that you are allowed to just *be* without being useful.",
